   "flagged": true,
   "statspai_version": "1.43.1",
   "mechanism": "Reference convention, wrong in this design. ivmediate (and the default here, which equals it to 1e-11) sets the covariance between coefficients of different equations to zero, so Var(a d) = d^2 V(a) + a^2 V(d). The mediator equation's error and the outcome equation's error share the component v, so cov(a, d) is not zero: it is negative when v enters the outcome with a positive loading (the SE is too large) and positive when the loading is negative (the SE is too small). equations='joint' keeps the covariance (rows iv_mediate.indirect.joint*; equal to Stata gmm + nlcom to 2e-12). The default is unchanged because it is the documented ivmediate number; changing it is an owner decision."
  },
